# Build context = the recipe, not the data.
#
# The image is a few hundred MB of Python and a copy of this repo; everything that
# makes the repo big is either a mount at run time (`/models`, `/app/results`) or
# an artefact of running it here. Two rules decide what stays:
#
#   * the container must be able to warm-start its expert arena offline, which needs
#     `results/*/stats/coverage.json` (about 1 MB) and nothing else from `results/`;
#   * the raw routing trace (`results/*/trace/*.npz`) and the tracer's resume state
#     (`results/*/state/`) are inputs to `tools/expert_stats.py`, never to the server.
#
# Compose bind-mounts ./results over /app/results anyway, so a box that has the full
# trace still sees it; what is excluded here only shrinks the image.

.git
.gitignore
.github/

# never in an image
.env
*.env
!env.example
models/
engram_rows/
logs/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.DS_Store

# large results: keep stats/, drop the raw trace and the resume state
results/*/trace/
results/*/state/
results/oneshots/

# docs travel with the repo, not with the runtime
docs/
CHANGELOG.md
CREDITS.md
NOTES.md
LIMITATIONS.md
RESULTS.md
